"settings.ambient.description" = "Hold Option and point at a diagram: FlowPeek outlines it and %@ opens it. Only reads while Option is down: what is under the pointer, and in an editor that exposes nothing there — VS Code and other Electron apps — the document it has open, anchored on the text cursor. Apps that draw their own text — a terminal rendering to a canvas, for one — expose nothing to read; copying still works there. It is a switch rather than always on: while it is on, that key belongs to FlowPeek instead of to whatever you are typing in.";
