"settings.terminal.short" = "A diagram printed in Terminal, iTerm2 or Ghostty gets a frame where it sits.";
"settings.detail" = "Details";
"settings.terminal.description" = "Print a diagram in Terminal, iTerm2 or Ghostty and FlowPeek draws a faint frame around it where it sits, one for each diagram on screen. Bring the pointer near and the frame brightens with a button that opens it; hold Option and the whole block opens on a click. Nothing to select, nothing to copy. It reads only while one of those three is in front, and the frame goes as soon as the block scrolls off screen. A terminal that draws its own text into a web view — Orca, VS Code’s built-in terminal, anything on xterm.js — exposes nothing to read; copying still works there.";
